        <item>
            <title>2.03</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 21:01:54 +0700</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif;margin:0;padding:0 4px}h2{font-size:20px;margin:6px 0 4px}h3{font-size:13px;margin:16px 0 4px}p{margin:4px 0}.date{opacity:.6}ul{margin:4px 0;padding-left:20px}li{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}</style></head><body><h2>2.03</h2><p class="date">Release date: 5 Oct 2026</p><h3>New in 2.03</h3><ul><li>Indexing no longer gets stuck while a Cursor or Codex session is running. A long log is read on from where the last scan stopped – a 200 MB Codex log took 33 s on every change, now under a millisecond.</li><li>Cursor, Codex and Gemini show "Indexing N of M" during the first scan.</li><li>Settings → the bug icon, bottom left, copies diagnostics to paste into a support email.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
